{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":7861384,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,11,7]],"date-time":"2026-11-07T08:18:25Z","timestamp":1794039505015,"version":"4.8.0"},"reference-count":14,"publisher":"AIP Publishing","issue":"4","content-domain":{"domain":["pubs.aip.org"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2001,7,22]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>The stochastic simulation algorithm (SSA) is an essentially exact procedure for numerically simulating the time evolution of a well-stirred chemically reacting system. Despite recent major improvements in the efficiency of the SSA, its drawback remains the great amount of computer time that is often required to simulate a desired amount of system time. Presented here is the \u201c\u03c4-leap\u201d method, an approximate procedure that in some circumstances can produce significant gains in simulation speed with acceptable losses in accuracy. Some primitive strategies for control parameter selection and error mitigation for the \u03c4-leap method are described, and simulation results for two simple model systems are exhibited. With further refinement, the \u03c4-leap method should provide a viable way of segueing from the exact SSA to the approximate chemical Langevin equation, and thence to the conventional deterministic reaction rate equation, as the system size becomes larger.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1063\/1.1378322","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2002,7,26]],"date-time":"2002-07-26T08:44:22Z","timestamp":1027673062000},"page":"1716-1733","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1063\/aip-crossmark-policy-page","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":1591,"title":["Approximate accelerated stochastic simulation of chemically reacting systems"],"prefix":"10.1063","volume":"115","author":[{"given":"Daniel T.","family":"Gillespie","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Research Department, Code 4T4100D, Naval Air Warfare Center, China Lake, California\u200993555"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"317","reference":[{"key":"2024021106394126800_r1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"403","DOI":"10.1016\/0021-9991(76)90041-3","volume":"22","year":"1976","journal-title":"J. Comput. Phys."},{"key":"2024021106394126800_r2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"2340","DOI":"10.1021\/j100540a008","volume":"81","year":"1977","journal-title":"J. Phys. Chem."},{"key":"2024021106394126800_r3","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"413","DOI":"10.2307\/3212214","volume":"4","year":"1967","journal-title":"J. Appl. Probab."},{"key":"2024021106394126800_r4","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"404","DOI":"10.1016\/0378-4371(92)90283-V","volume":"188","year":"1992","journal-title":"Physica A"},{"key":"2024021106394126800_r5","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"814","DOI":"10.1073\/pnas.94.3.814","volume":"94","year":"1997","journal-title":"Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. U.S.A."},{"key":"2024021106394126800_r6","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1633","DOI":"10.1093\/genetics\/149.4.1633","volume":"149","year":"1998","journal-title":"Genetics"},{"key":"2024021106394126800_r7","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"2598","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevE.58.2598","volume":"58","year":"1998","journal-title":"Phys. Rev. E"},{"key":"2024021106394126800_r8","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1876","DOI":"10.1021\/jp993732q","volume":"104","year":"2000","journal-title":"J. Phys. Chem. A"},{"key":"2024021106394126800_r9","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"391","DOI":"10.1038\/35053181","volume":"409","year":"2001","journal-title":"Nature (London)"},{"key":"2024021106394126800_r10","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"297","DOI":"10.1063\/1.481811","volume":"113","year":"2000","journal-title":"J. Chem. Phys."},{"key":"2024021106394126800_r11"},{"key":"2024021106394126800_r12"},{"key":"2024021106394126800_r13"},{"key":"2024021106394126800_r14"}],"container-title":["The Journal of Chemical Physics"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/pubs.aip.org\/aip\/jcp\/article-pdf\/115\/4\/1716\/19076619\/1716_1_online.pdf","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"syndication"},{"URL":"https:\/\/pubs.aip.org\/aip\/jcp\/article-pdf\/115\/4\/1716\/19076619\/1716_1_online.pdf","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,2,11]],"date-time":"2024-02-11T01:39:53Z","timestamp":1707615593000},"score":69.56567,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/pubs.aip.org\/jcp\/article\/115\/4\/1716\/451187\/Approximate-accelerated-stochastic-simulation-of"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2001,7,22]]},"references-count":14,"journal-issue":{"issue":"4","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2001,7,22]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1063\/1.1378322","ISSN":["0021-9606","1089-7690"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0021-9606","type":"print"},{"value":"1089-7690","type":"electronic"}],"published-other":{"date-parts":[[2001,7,22]]},"published":{"date-parts":[[2001,7,22]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,6]],"date-time":"2026-05-06T07:46:09Z","timestamp":1778053569214,"version":"3.51.4"},"reference-count":33,"publisher":"AIP Publishing","issue":"1","content-domain":{"domain":["pubs.aip.org"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2012,1,7]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>In recent years, computer simulations have become increasingly useful when trying to understand the complex dynamics of biochemical networks, particularly in stochastic systems. In such situations stochastic simulation is vital in gaining an understanding of the inherent stochasticity present, as these models are rarely analytically tractable. However, a stochastic approach can be computationally prohibitive for many models. A number of approximations have been proposed that aim to speed up stochastic simulations. However, the majority of these approaches are fundamentally serial in terms of central processing unit (CPU) usage. In this paper, we propose a novel simulation algorithm that utilises the potential of multi-core machines. This algorithm partitions the model into smaller sub-models. These sub-models are then simulated, in parallel, on separate CPUs. We demonstrate that this method is accurate and can speed-up the simulation by a factor proportional to the number of processors available.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1063\/1.3670416","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2012,1,4]],"date-time":"2012-01-04T02:19:30Z","timestamp":1325643570000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1063\/aip-crossmark-policy-page","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":5,"title":["Stochastic simulation of chemically reacting systems using multi-core processors"],"prefix":"10.1063","volume":"136","author":[{"given":"Colin S.","family":"Gillespie","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Newcastle University School of Mathematics & Statistics, , Newcastle upon Tyne, NE1 7RU, United Kingdom"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"317","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2012,1,3]]},"reference":[{"key":"2023062522265082300_c1","first-page":"177","volume-title":"Essays in Biochemistry \u2013 Systems Biology","author":"Wolkenhauer","year":"2008"},{"key":"2023062522265082300_c2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"391","DOI":"10.1038\/35053181","volume":"409","year":"2001","journal-title":"Nature (London)"},{"key":"2023062522265082300_c3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"206","DOI":"10.1038\/nature01254","volume":"420","year":"2002","journal-title":"Nature (London)"},{"key":"2023062522265082300_c4","first-page":"53","volume-title":"Computational Cell Biology","author":"Fall","year":"2005","edition":"3rd"},{"key":"2023062522265082300_c5","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1633","DOI":"10.1093\/genetics\/149.4.1633","volume":"149","y